('Allied Health Sciences', 'Human Nutrition and Dietetics', 'competency', 'explain-programme-ideas', 'Explain the programme''s main ideas', 'This means being able to describe the key ideas in Human Nutrition and Dietetics in your own words and connect them to the course topics.', 'Build this after orientation so the student can tell the difference between memorising course titles and understanding what the programme does.', 'A short explanation, comparison, diagram, calculation, design, experiment, case analysis or other output appropriate to the programme.', 'build_next', 'Build this next because the CCMAS outcomes move from subject knowledge into understanding and application.', '["Understand Human Nutrition and Dietetics"]'::jsonb, '["apply-programme-learning"]'::jsonb, ARRAY['nuc_ccmas','open_reference_allied-health-sciences']::text[], '[{"id":"nuc_ccmas","title":"NUC CCMAS source page","url":"https://www.nuc.edu.ng/ccmas/","region":"nigeria","evidenceType":"official_curriculum_source"},{"id":"open_reference_allied-health-sciences","title":"Anatomy and Physiology 2e","url":"https://openstax.org/books/anatomy-and-physiology-2e/pages/1-introduction","region":"global","evidenceType":"free_foundation_reference"}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceFile":"allied_health.json","originalPdf":"Allied-Health-Sciences-2023.pdf","courseCode":"NUT 101","courseTitle":"Introduction to Human Nutrition and Dietetics","level":100},{"sourceFile":"allied_health.json","originalPdf":"Allied-Health-Sciences-2023.pdf","courseCode":"NUT 201","courseTitle":"Principles of Nutrition and Dietetics","level":200},{"sourceFile":"allied_health.json","originalPdf":"Allied-Health-Sciences-2023.pdf","courseCode":"NUT 202","courseTitle":"Introduction to Clinical Nutrition","level":200},{"sourceFile":"allied_health.json","originalPdf":"Allied-Health-Sciences-2023.pdf","courseCode":"NUT 301","courseTitle":"Food Composition, Analysis & Sensory Evaluation","level":300},{"sourceFile":"allied_health.json","originalPdf":