('Law', 'Law', 'competency', 'explain-programme-ideas', 'Explain the programme''s main ideas', 'This means being able to describe the key ideas in Law in your own words and connect them to the course topics.', 'Build this after orientation so the student can tell the difference between memorising course titles and understanding what the programme does.', 'A short explanation, comparison, diagram, calculation, design, experiment, case analysis or other output appropriate to the programme.', 'build_next', 'Build this next because the CCMAS outcomes move from subject knowledge into understanding and application.', '["Understand Law"]'::jsonb, '["apply-programme-learning"]'::jsonb, ARRAY['nuc_ccmas','open_reference_law']::text[], '[{"id":"nuc_ccmas","title":"NUC CCMAS source page","url":"https://www.nuc.edu.ng/ccmas/","region":"nigeria","evidenceType":"official_curriculum_source"},{"id":"open_reference_law","title":"Business Law and the Legal Environment","url":"https://open.umn.edu/opentextbooks/textbooks/business-law-and-the-legal-environment","region":"global","evidenceType":"free_foundation_reference"}]'::jsonb, '[{"sourceFile":"law.json","originalPdf":"Law-ALL.pdf","courseCode":"GST 111","courseTitle":"Communication in English","level":100},{"sourceFile":"law.json","originalPdf":"Law-ALL.pdf","courseCode":"GST 112","courseTitle":"Nigerian Peoples and Culture","level":100},{"sourceFile":"law.json","originalPdf":"Law-ALL.pdf","courseCode":"PSY 101","courseTitle":"Introduction to Psychology","level":100},{"sourceFile":"law.json","originalPdf":"Law-ALL.pdf","courseCode":"PHL 105","courseTitle":"Introduction to Social and Political Philosophy","level":100},{"sourceFile":"law.json","originalPdf":"Law-ALL.pdf","courseCode":"PUL 101","courseTitle":"Legal Methods I","level":100},{"sourceFile":"law.json","originalPdf":"Law-ALL.pdf","courseCode":"PUL 102","courseTitle":"Legal Methods II","level":100},{"sourceFile":"law.json","originalPdf":"Law-ALL.pdf","courseCode":"LAW 101",